      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name 'Acoma' translates to 'a place that always was' in the Keres language, underscoring the indigenous view of the land as an eternal homeland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/south_acomita_village_new_mexico",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "South Acomita Village experiences a semi‑arid steppe climate, with hot summers, cold winters, and low humidity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/south_acomita_village_new_mexico",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Erosion along the Rio San Jose, driven by episodic fluvial activity, creates high sediment loads and valley instability.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/south_acomita_village_new_mexico",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "South Acomita Village exemplifies the Acoma reservation’s role in preserving Native American heritage amid contemporary challenges like water rights and community development.",
